      "text": "# Safe Offline Archive Importer\n\n## Design Overview\n\nThis implementation provides a secure, robust ZIP archive importer that addresses common security vulnerabilities and reliability concerns when extracting archives from untrusted sources. The key design principles are:\n\n1. **Path Normalization & Traversal Prevention**: Reject any entry whose normalized path escapes the target directory\n2. **Symlink/Link Safety**: Never create symlinks or hardlinks; treat them as regular files or reject them\n3. **Size Limits**: Enforce maximum uncompressed size, compressed size, and total extracted size to prevent zip bombs\n4. **Streaming Extraction**: Process entries incrementally without loading entire files into memory\n5. **Atomic Publication**: Extract to a temporary directory, then atomically move to final location\n6. **Interrupted Extraction Handling**: Use journaling/checkpointing to allow resumption or clean rollback\n\n## Security Threats Addressed\n\n| Threat | Mitigation |\n|--------|-----------|\n| Path traversal (`../../etc/passwd`) | Normalize paths, reject absolute paths and `..` components |\n| Zip bomb (huge uncompressed size) | Enforce per-file and total size limits |\n| Symlink attacks | Never create symlinks; reject entries with symlink attributes |\n| Partial extraction on crash | Atomic rename after full extraction; cleanup on failure |\n| Resource exhaustion | Streaming I/O, bounded buffers, size checks before allocation |\n| Unicode normalization attacks | Normalize filenames, reject control characters |\n\n## Implementation\n\n```python\n\"\"\"\nSafe offline archive importer for ZIP files.\n\nThis module provides a secure ZIP extraction utility that protects against\ncommon archive-based attacks including path traversal, zip bombs, symlink\nattacks, and resource exhaustion.\n\nKey features:\n- Path normalization and traversal prevention\n- Symlink/hardlink rejection\n- Configurable size limits (per-file, total, compressed)\n- Streaming extraction with bounded memory usage\n- Atomic publication via temporary directory + rename\n- Interrupted extraction detection and cleanup\n\"\"\"\n\nimport binascii\nimport io\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport stat\nimport struct\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport threading\nimport time\nimport warnings\nfrom pathlib import Path, PurePosixPath\nfrom typing import Optional, Iterator, BinaryIO, Tuple, Set, Dict, Any\n\n# Try to import compression modules\ntry:\n    import zlib\n    crc32 = zlib.crc32\nexcept ImportError:\n    zlib = None\n    crc32 = binascii.crc32\n\ntry:\n    import bz2\nexcept ImportError:\n    bz2 = None\n\ntry:\n    import lzma\nexcept ImportError:\n    lzma = None\n\ntry:\n    from compression import zstd\nexcept ImportError:\n    zstd = None\n\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"SafeZipImporter\",\n    \"ImportError\",\n    \"PathTraversalError\",\n    \"SizeLimitExceededError\",\n    \"SymlinkError\",\n    \"CorruptArchiveError\",\n    \"ImportResult\",\n]\n\n\nclass ImportError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for safe import errors.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass PathTraversalError(ImportError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an archive entry attempts to escape the target directory.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass SizeLimitExceededError(ImportError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an archive entry exceeds configured size limits.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass SymlinkError(ImportError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an archive entry contains a symlink or hardlink.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass CorruptArchiveError(ImportError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when the archive is malformed or unreadable.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass ImportResult:\n    \"\"\"Result of a safe import operation.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.extracted_files: list[str] = []\n        self.skipped_files: list[str] = []\n        self.total_bytes_extracted: int = 0\n        self.total_files: int = 0\n        self.errors: list[str] = []\n        self.interrupted: bool = False\n        self.interruption_reason: Optional[str] = None\n\n    def __repr__(self):\n        return (\n            f\"ImportResult(extracted={len(self.extracted_files)}, \"\n            f\"skipped={len(self.skipped_files)}, \"\n            f\"bytes={self.total_bytes_extracted}, \"\n            f\"interrupted={self.interrupted})\"\n        )\n\n\n# ZIP format constants (from reference implementation)\nZIP_STORED = 0\nZIP_DEFLATED = 8\nZIP_BZIP2 = 12\nZIP_LZMA = 14\nZIP_ZSTANDARD = 93\n\n# End of central directory\nstructEndArchive = b\"<4s4H2LH\"\nstringEndArchive = b\"PK\\005\\006\"\nsizeEndCentDir",
